   "ble_spam_apple": {
    "v": "yes",
    "note": "Apple Continuity. BLE Spam ORIGINATED in Xtreme before moving to Momentum. Historical: as of the 2024 release, and largely mitigated by vendors since. Real, but oversold. The STM32WB55 BLE stack advertises one payload at a time and cycles through them, so this is protocol-level nuisance advertising, not RF jamming and not a flood. Apple (iOS 17.2+), Google, Microsoft and Samsung all added cooldowns and sanity checks after 2023, so on current phones it is mostly a party trick. The app's own author describes it that way."
   },
