  "stealth": "discreet",
  "form_factor": "board",
  "summary": "Ghost ESP was an ESP-IDF Wi-Fi and BLE pentest firmware with a web UI, a serial command line and a Flipper Zero companion app, covering scanning, deauth, beacon spam, evil portals, wardriving and some novelty attacks against Chromecast/DIAL and TP-Link devices. Its maintainer archived it in April 2025.",
  "honest_take": "Do not start here. The repo is archived and the README says outright that the project is dead and will not return, the last release was March 2025, and the maintainer has since moved on to unrelated projects. Its 230 forks contain nobody with meaningful traction - every actively-pushed fork has zero stars - so there is no successor to migrate to. Anything Ghost ESP did, ESP32 Marauder and Bruce both still do, on the same hardware, with active maintenance. The only reason to touch it now is historical curiosity or because you already have a device with it flashed. Its genuinely distinctive bits - the DIAL/Chromecast casting attack and the TP-Link smart-device probe - are the parts no maintained firmware directly replaced. Its Wi-Fi attacks were also frozen in 2025, before this mattered as much: deauth is defeated by 802.11w/PMF, which WPA3 makes mandatory, and nobody is going to update this firmware to work around that.",
