  "honest_take": "Both halves of this pairing are end-of-line: Ghost ESP was archived by its maintainer with a note saying it is never coming back, and M5Stack has EOL'd this Cardputer revision in favour of the Adv. If you own this combination it still works, but there is no upgrade path on either side. The same board runs Bruce, which is actively maintained and strictly more capable, and reflashing takes minutes - there is no good reason to stay on Ghost ESP. Worth noting the original Cardputer has no PSRAM at all, so packet capture was always constrained here. The frozen firmware also means frozen limitations - its deauth is defeated by 802.11w/PMF, which WPA3 makes mandatory, and that will never be revisited here.",
