   "notes": "Higher risk than a scanning tool because the whole design goal is capturing other people's credentials. Running an Evil-Twin or KARMA attack means impersonating someone else's network and inducing their devices to connect to yours, which is generally an offence quite separate from deauthentication, and the captured credentials are personal data you are then holding. The author's own disclaimer restricts it to controlled environments. Note also the repo has no licence, so redistributing or building products on it is legally murky. Only use under a written, scoped engagement. Check your local law."
