  "summary": "A USB-A-plug ESP32-S3 board with a 1.47-inch 172x320 colour LCD, 16MB flash and 8MB of Octal PSRAM, and a microSD slot on a 4-bit bus. Under USB Army Knife it does the full platform: HID injection, mass storage, USB Ethernet and the embedded Marauder, with the best screen and most RAM of the supported dongles.",
  "honest_take": "On paper this is the best-specified USB Army Knife board - 8MB PSRAM against the T-Dongle-S3's none, a much larger screen, and a 4-bit SD bus rather than SPI. The catch is presentation: it is a bare PCB with exposed circuitry on the underside and an acrylic front layer, so it looks like a project, not a memory stick, which undercuts the covertness that makes these tools interesting. There is no battery or charging circuit, so it only lives while plugged in. If you want the capability and do not need to hide it, this is the pick; if you need it to look innocuous, the cased ESP32-S3-GEEK or the T-Dongle-S3 are better. Watch out for the sibling models - the 1.47B adds an IMU and battery charging, and a separate Touch variant exists. The Wi-Fi side carries the usual caveat - deauth is defeated by 802.11w/PMF, which WPA3 makes mandatory - so the USB attack surface, not the radio, is the reason to own one.",
